## 🚀 Project Overview

SparkCV is an enterprise-grade AI resume ecosystem designed to bridge the gap between candidate talent and Applicant Tracking System (ATS) algorithms. Unlike generic builders, SparkCV focuses on **quantifiable impact** and **structural integrity**, ensuring resumes are not only visually professional but computationally optimized for recruiter discovery.

By integrating state-of-the-art LLMs and a rigorous PDF rendering pipeline, SparkCV empowers job seekers to convert static work histories into dynamic, high-impact narratives that statistically increase interview rates.

## ✨ Core Engineering Features

### 🛠️ Precision Resume Builder
- **Dynamic Narrative Engine**: A sophisticated drag-and-drop interface with real-time preview.
- **Rich Text Bullet Integration**: Advanced `BulletPointsEditor` supporting structured, multi-point experience descriptions, replacing flat text with high-impact achievement lists.
- **Dynamic Hyperlinking**: Integrated support for dynamic links, allowing candidates to embed portfolios, GitHub repositories, and LinkedIn profiles directly into the PDF.
- **Typography Suite**: Professional-grade font customization, including the addition of **Computer Modern Serif Roman** for a classic, academic, and high-authority aesthetic.

### 🤖 AI Intelligence Layer
- **Provider-Agnostic Architecture**: A robust AI integration layer supporting **Google Gemini** and any **OpenAI-compatible** providers, ensuring zero vendor lock-in and maximum uptime.
- **Impact-Driven Enhancement**: AI-powered phrasing that shifts descriptions from "responsible for" (passive) to "achieved X by doing Y, resulting in Z" (quantifiable).
- **Robust JSON Orchestration**: Enhanced AI response handling and a hardened JSON parser to ensure stable, structured data extraction from LLM outputs.

### 📊 ATS Engineering & Scoring
- **Serverless Text Extraction**: Migrated to `unpdf` for stable, high-performance PDF text extraction in serverless environments, eliminating the overhead of headless browsers.
- **Gap Analysis Algorithm**: Instant resume analysis against job descriptions, providing a quantifiable match score and a precise keyword delta to optimize for specific roles.
- **Tailored Cover Letter Engine**: Context-aware generation that synthesizes resume data and job requirements into high-conversion cover letters.

### 📄 Production-Grade Export
- **ATS-Compliant PDF Pipeline**: Powered by `@react-pdf/renderer`, producing text-selectable, structurally sound PDFs that maintain 100% fidelity between preview and export.
- **High-Fidelity Rendering**: Specialized handling of bullet points and complex layouts to ensure seamless parsing by legacy and modern ATS software.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Engineering Justification |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Framework** | Next.js 16 (App Router) | Utilizes React Server Components (RSC) and Server Actions to minimize client-side JS and reduce Time-to-Interactive (TTI). |
| **Language** | TypeScript 5.9 | Enforces strict type safety across the AI-to-DB pipeline, reducing runtime errors in complex resume schemas. |
| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS v4 & Radix UI | Utility-first styling paired with accessible primitives for a premium, responsive, and accessible user interface. |
| **Database** | PostgreSQL (Neon) & Prisma | Serverless PostgreSQL with connection pooling via Prisma ORM for scalable, type-safe data persistence. |
| **Authentication**| Clerk | Enterprise-grade identity management with seamless OAuth and session synchronization. |
| **Payments** | Stripe | Robust subscription lifecycle management (Free, Pro, Pro Plus) via secure webhooks. |
| **AI Core** | Google Gemini / OpenAI | Multi-model support for high-reasoning ATS analysis and rapid text generation. |
| **State Mgt** | Zustand | Lightweight, atomic state management for the high-frequency updates required by the drag-and-drop editor. |
| **PDF Engine** | `@react-pdf/renderer` | Client-side and server-side PDF generation ensuring ATS readability without headless browser overhead. |

